SNAPACK Hardware Specification

Status: Authoritative
Revision: Draft 1

============================================================
PURPOSE
============================================================

This Specification Defines The Hardware Protection
Systems Incorporated Into SNAPACK.

It Covers:

• Hardware Fault Detection
• ADS1115 ALERT Circuit
• Authorization Interruption
• Temperature Protection Support
• Reverse Current Protection Support

Electrical Connections Are Defined In:

    01_Authoritative_Pin_Mapping.txt

============================================================
SYSTEM OVERVIEW
============================================================

SNAPACK Uses Independent Hardware Protection
Circuits To Interrupt The Positive Authorization
Circuit When A Protection Condition Exists.

The Protection Hardware Operates Independently
Of The Main High Current Switching Components.

============================================================
HARDWARE
============================================================

Fault Detection

ADS1115 ALERT Output

------------------------------------------------------------

Protection Relay

AITRIP 5V Single Channel
Opto-Isolated Relay Module

Quantity

1

============================================================
AUTHORIZATION CIRCUIT
============================================================

The Positive Authorization Circuit Passes
Through The Opto-Isolated Relay Module.

Removal Of Authorization Prevents Contactor
Operation.

============================================================
SUPPORTED PROTECTION FUNCTIONS
============================================================

Hardware Supports

• Over Temperature Shutdown

• Reverse Charge Protection

• Sensor Fault Response

• Manual Emergency Shutdown

• Controller Initiated Shutdown

============================================================
TEMPERATURE SUPPORT
============================================================

Temperature Hardware Provides The Information
Required To Support Automatic Cold Charge
Protection.

Protection Logic Is Defined In

Software Manifest

============================================================
CURRENT SUPPORT
============================================================

Current Measurement Hardware Provides The
Information Required To Detect Reverse Current.

Protection Logic Is Defined In

Software Manifest

============================================================
FAULT INDICATION
============================================================

Hardware Fault Status May Be Presented To

• Display

• RGB Status Ring

• Relay Output

============================================================
VERIFICATION
============================================================

Verify

□ ADS1115 ALERT Operation

□ Opto Relay Operation

□ Authorization Interruption

□ Manual Shutdown

□ Fault Indication

□ System Recovery

